v056ped5@ubvmsd.cc.buffalo.edu (Brian M McNamara) writes:

{B} This is not really a bug, but a step down in quality. For some reason I
{B} keep getting a screen flicker everytime a store is encountered. I do not
{B} know why and it does not seem to do any damage, but it is irritating.

I had noticed that too.  It seems to occur on all machine types (not just
the PC).  The reason for it is that some of the screen redraw optimisation
was removed in pl 10 to fix a color bug (for machines with color like the
PC).

The bug appeared when you move off a square and a monster of the same
symbol (eg '@' or 'D' (if polymorphed)) moved onto that square the color was
not updated properly.  The quick fix was to remove some of the optimisation
(bug found *very* late in pl 10 coding).  I hear that the Dev Team has
better solutions for 3.1.

One possible way to get 'less flicker' on your screen is to get a different
ANSI.SYS driver for your PC.  The standard DOS ANSI.SYS *really* slows down
screen I/O.  I (personally) use the NNANSI.SYS 2.3 that was posted to
comp.binaries.ibm.pc a while back.  It is *much* faster and probably will
eliminate that problem for you.

{B} Also, most compilers have a routine to catch control characters. Is it 
